1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:03,461
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:12,929
[Diego] <i>Who are you, Ivy Aguas?</i>

3
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:15,432
<i>You never told me anything</i>
<i>about your family.</i>

4
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:18,226
<i>It's like you don't want</i>
<i>anyone entering your world.</i>

5
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:20,061
[Tonio] <i>I only killed the victims.</i>

6
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,730
<i>But I'm not the one who buried them.</i>

7
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:23,106
<i>-Who did?</i>
-[Tonio] <i>It's Noel.</i>

8
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:24,774
<i>Who ordered you to do it?</i>

9
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:26,901
<i>It was Raul. Raul Torillo.</i>

10
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:30,447
[Ivy] <i>Raul, you monster!</i>
<i>You wretched bastard!</i>

11
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:33,491
<i>Get ready, Raul, because</i>
<i>I'm going to take my mom back.</i>

12
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:36,745
[Raul] <i>I'm already packing our things.</i>

13
00:00:36,828 --> 00:00:39,164
<i>We're going to move somewhere else.</i>

14
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:40,707
[Julio] <i>Who told you</i>

15
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:43,835
<i>to take over everything I left behind?</i>

16
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:46,921
<i>You have no right sitting</i>

17
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:49,299
<i>-in my goddamn chair!</i>
-[glass shatters]

18
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:51,676
[Arnaldo] <i>Our beloved congressman,</i>

19
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:54,179
<i>Señor Julio Ardiente, will return!</i>

20
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:56,723
[Emilia] <i>I'll treat him like</i>
<i>one of my enemies.</i>

21
00:00:56,806 --> 00:00:58,308
<i>You're going to have Julio killed?</i>

22
00:00:58,391 --> 00:01:02,145
<i>Poblacion Ardiente is too small</i>
<i>for the both of us.</i>

23
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:04,856
[Ivy] <i>How did Lily</i>
<i>and her family disappear?</i>

24
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:07,776
<i>All I remember is her parents</i>
<i>had a fight with my dad.</i>

25
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:10,070
<i>I guess they left because</i>
<i>they didn't want any trouble.</i>

26
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:11,863
<i>It's like she's keeping something from me.</i>

27
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:13,615
<i>What do you think it is?</i>

28
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:14,532
<i>I don't know,</i>

29
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:17,452
<i>but I want to know her more</i>
<i>because I love her, Nanny.</i>

30
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:18,495
<i>What?!</i>

31
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:20,080
[Ivy] <i>It's your son's birthday.</i>

32
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:22,832
-<i>Yeah, I know.</i>
-[Ivy] <i>So, let's have fun?</i>

33
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:24,584
<i>Hello?</i>

34
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:29,255
<i>Hello? Are you with Camia Cruz?</i>
<i>Hello? Hello?</i>

35
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:31,800
Hello?

36
00:01:34,803 --> 00:01:36,596
[somber music playing]

37
00:01:36,679 --> 00:01:37,806
Hello?

38
00:01:54,531 --> 00:01:56,741
Jasmin? What are you doing?

39
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,494
Don't touch that. Come here.

40
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:01,538
You better rest in your room now.

41
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:03,706
[emotional music playing]

42
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:08,795
Go on.

43
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:11,381
Hurry up.

44
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:19,139
Ivy?

45
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:21,474
Is everything all right?

46
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:26,437
Why is my husband's phone with you?

47
00:02:27,772 --> 00:02:30,066
[tense music playing]

48
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:36,781
Oh, you're right!
I thought it was mine, Emilia.

49
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:39,200
I was talking to Mr. Torillo earlier.

50
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:41,411
Tell him not to leave
his phone lying around

51
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:46,541
because someone might take it from him.

52
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:52,046
Thanks for the advice, Ivy.

53
00:02:52,505 --> 00:02:55,133
We really should cut off the hands of…

54
00:02:57,051 --> 00:02:58,553
cell phone thieves.

55
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:09,689
[Emilia clears throat]

56
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:12,233
So, did--

57
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:14,861
So, you're waiting for someone.

58
00:03:15,778 --> 00:03:19,240
No. I just asked the waiter
to bring me a drink.

59
00:03:19,407 --> 00:03:20,533
Here's your phone.

60
00:03:22,118 --> 00:03:23,286
Where did you get this?

61
00:03:23,661 --> 00:03:24,954
From Miss Aguas.

62
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:34,589
You know what? I was wondering
why Miss Aguas had your phone.

63
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:36,382
Any thoughts?

64
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:38,051
I don't know either, Emilia.

65
00:03:43,014 --> 00:03:44,807
You lying bastard.

66
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:48,144
[tense music playing]

67
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:55,777
[upbeat music playing]

68
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:58,947
Ladies and gentlemen,

69
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:00,782
may I have your attention, please?

70
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:05,119
I'd like to propose a toast for Arnaldo.

71
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:08,706
Mayor Arnaldo,
can you please join me here?

72
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:10,541
Sure. Excuse me.

73
00:04:12,126 --> 00:04:15,213
How about a big hand
for my son, Mayor Arnaldo?

74
00:04:15,296 --> 00:04:17,048
-[applause]
-Thank you. Thank you.

75
00:04:17,173 --> 00:04:19,425
Arnaldo, happy, happy birthday.

76
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:23,721
I wish you all the best
and may you continue to shine

77
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:27,141
for the people of Ardiente.
Happy birthday, son. I love you.

78
00:04:27,225 --> 00:04:28,393
Thank you very much.

79
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,479
-Cheers!
-[guests] Cheers!

80
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:33,564
-[glasses clink]
-[woman] Happy birthday, Mayor!

81
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:34,941
[Emilia] Happy birthday, Mayor.

82
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:36,276
-[Arnaldo] Thank you!
-[Emilia] A round of applause

83
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:37,527
for Mayor Arnaldo.

84
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:38,987
[applause]

85
00:04:39,737 --> 00:04:40,863
[Arnaldo] Thank you, Mom.

86
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:43,199
Thank you very much
for coming to my party.

87
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:45,994
But for now, I'd like to request everyone

88
00:04:46,077 --> 00:04:48,621
to turn your attention to the big screen.

89
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:52,250
There's an important person
who wants to join our party.

90
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:56,754
-[suspenseful sting]
-<i>Happy, happy birthday,</i>

91
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:59,382
<i>my favorite grandson.</i>

92
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:02,051
[suspenseful music playing]

93
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:14,605
Thank you very much, Grandpa!
How are you there in the States?

94
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:18,026
<i>I'm good. And you should</i>
<i>stop worrying about me.</i>

95
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:24,324
<i>Nothing can kill me here</i>
<i>in America, aside from my heart.</i>

96
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:25,491
[laughs]

97
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:26,993
That's a bad joke, Grandpa.

98
00:05:27,076 --> 00:05:30,121
I just want to make sure
that everything is all right.

99
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:37,670
<i>Remember, Arnaldo.</i>
<i>No one can bring me down.</i>

100
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:43,092
<i>And once I return to Poblacion Ardiente…</i>

101
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:47,263
<i>I will clean up all the trash</i>

102
00:05:47,346 --> 00:05:50,725
<i>that gathered there while I was away.</i>

103
00:05:50,808 --> 00:05:55,438
[dramatic music playing]

104
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:05,364
<i>You know who you are,</i>
<i>and I'll be seeing you soon.</i>

105
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:16,334
Ladies and gentlemen, that's
Congressman Julio Ardiente!

106
00:06:16,417 --> 00:06:18,586
[applause]

107
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:20,922
[Arnaldo] Okay. Well,
let's go back to the party.

108
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:22,131
Thank you very much!

109
00:06:27,804 --> 00:06:30,515
[suspenseful music playing]

110
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:43,736
Ivy? Ivy! Ivy! Ivy, wait.

111
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:46,572
Diego.

112
00:06:46,656 --> 00:06:48,658
I just want to apologize
for what I did earlier.

113
00:06:50,201 --> 00:06:52,203
It's fine. I understand.
Sorry, I have to go.

114
00:06:52,286 --> 00:06:53,162
Wait.

115
00:06:54,372 --> 00:06:57,625
I just want to explain
why I did all that earlier.

116
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:59,544
Diego, it's fine.
You don't have to explain.

117
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:00,795
Ivy, you have to listen to me.

118
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:02,255
Please, Diego. I don't have time for this.

119
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:04,757
We can talk some other time.

120
00:07:05,049 --> 00:07:06,217
Sorry, I have to go.

121
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,385
Ivy…

122
00:07:08,761 --> 00:07:09,971
[somber guitar music playing]

123
00:07:10,054 --> 00:07:12,348
<i>No matter how long it takes,</i>
<i>I'll wait for you, Ivy.</i>

124
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:14,725
<i>Because I love you.</i>

125
00:07:20,064 --> 00:07:22,608
[unsettling music playing]

126
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:28,656
[Ivy] <i>Hello, are you with Camia Cruz?</i>

127
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:35,288
[echoing] <i>Camia Cruz.</i>
<i>Camia Cruz. Camia Cruz.</i>

128
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:45,798
<i>Atty. Dante Cruz.</i>
<i>This is my daughter, Lily.</i>

129
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:47,133
<i>And my wife, Camia.</i>

130
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:49,719
[unsettling music playing]

131
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:02,148
[suspenseful music playing]

132
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:21,709
[suspenseful music playing]

133
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:32,470
[engine starts]

134
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:43,481
[dark piano music playing]

135
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:47,902
[sobbing]

136
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:51,948
-[screams]
-[glass shatters]

137
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:54,367
[breathing heavily]

138
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:56,744
Emilia!

139
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:04,377
Auntie, Papa is alive and well.

140
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:09,257
I don't understand!
Why can't he just die?!

141
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:12,718
Weeds are hard to get rid of, Emilia.

142
00:09:13,886 --> 00:09:15,429
[exhales sharply, sniffles]

143
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:19,850
But, Auntie, I don't understand.

144
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:21,644
[sniffles]

145
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:29,986
He will regret coming back here
to Poblacion Ardiente.

146
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:35,491
I will make his life a living hell.

147
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:39,704
[dramatic music playing]

148
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:59,765
[Belen] Jasmin! Your food is ready!

149
00:10:00,641 --> 00:10:01,934
I'm coming in, okay?

150
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:12,320
Asleep again?

151
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:15,114
I'll just leave your food here.

152
00:10:16,782 --> 00:10:17,825
[suspenseful music playing]

153
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:20,077
[Belen] Just eat when you feel like it.

154
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:22,371
-[glass shatters]
-[screams in pain]

155
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:24,957
[Belen whimpering]

156
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:31,797
[Belen] Jasmin! Jasmin! Jasmin!

157
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:35,259
Jasmin! Jasmin!

158
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:38,804
Jasmin!

159
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:46,103
[suspenseful music playing]

160
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:59,825
[pants, screams]

161
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:04,664
[screams]

162
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:06,791
[car horn honking]

163
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,128
[suspenseful music playing]

164
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:23,432
[panting]

165
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:25,601
-[horn honking]
-[yelps]

166
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:30,064
[suspenseful music playing]

167
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:49,542
[suspenseful music playing]

168
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:56,424
[tires screech]

169
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:03,139
[suspenseful music intensifies]

170
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:12,731
Mom?

171
00:12:24,326 --> 00:12:25,244
Mom?

172
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:27,746
[somber music playing]

173
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:34,503
Mom?!

174
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:35,963
Mom!

175
00:12:36,922 --> 00:12:37,923
Mom!

176
00:12:38,716 --> 00:12:39,717
Mom!

177
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:43,304
-[Raul] Auntie? Auntie.
-[Belen crying] Raul.

178
00:12:43,387 --> 00:12:44,722
-Auntie.
-Raul.

179
00:12:45,264 --> 00:12:46,849
-What happened to you?
-Jasmin got away.

180
00:12:46,932 --> 00:12:47,933
-What?!
-Jasmin ran away!

181
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:51,061
-Where is Jasmin?!
-Look for her! Find her.

182
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:57,526
[gloomy music playing]

183
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:04,783
Mom! Mom, where are you? Mom!

184
00:13:07,786 --> 00:13:09,747
Mom, don't be scared.

185
00:13:12,666 --> 00:13:14,126
Mom, I'm your daughter!

186
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:16,212
Mom!

187
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:22,551
[pensive music playing]

188
00:13:29,099 --> 00:13:30,184
[young Lily] <i>Mom?</i>

189
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:33,479
[Camia] <i>Go on. Hurry. Get out of here.</i>

190
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:43,280
Mom! Mom, wait! Mom! Mom!

191
00:13:45,282 --> 00:13:47,368
[line ringing]

192
00:13:47,451 --> 00:13:49,578
[tense music playing]

193
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:55,251
[line ringing]

194
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:59,505
Madrigal, where have you been?
I haven't seen you around.

195
00:14:00,214 --> 00:14:02,299
I was in the area, Mayor.
I was just outside.

196
00:14:04,009 --> 00:14:05,052
Have you seen Miss Aguas?

197
00:14:05,135 --> 00:14:07,054
I've been looking for her.
She's not answering her phone.

198
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:09,890
I haven't seen her, Mayor.

199
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:12,643
[exhales sharply] Where is she?

200
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:13,727
[tense music playing]

201
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:16,063
Look for Miss Aguas. Now. Go!

202
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:38,627
Mom! Mom, wait! Mom, wait!
Mom, it's me, Lily!

203
00:14:38,794 --> 00:14:40,337
[panting]

204
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:45,843
Mom, it's me, your daughter, Lily.

205
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,511
[panting]

206
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:49,763
Wait! Don't leave.

207
00:14:51,473 --> 00:14:52,558
Mom…

208
00:14:56,228 --> 00:14:58,063
Mom! Mom!

209
00:14:58,731 --> 00:14:59,773
[tires screech]

210
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:02,443
Mom!

211
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:07,197
[screams]

212
00:15:11,243 --> 00:15:14,663
My mom… That was my mom.

213
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:18,959
[instrumental theme music playing]

214
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:20,628
My mom is alive.

215
00:15:21,962 --> 00:15:23,047
[exhales]

216
00:15:25,215 --> 00:15:26,842
But why did she run?

217
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:39,021
[panting]

218
00:15:39,396 --> 00:15:42,733
[suspenseful music playing]

219
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:48,781
-[Camia exclaims, cries]
-[shushes]

220
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:03,212
Arnaldo, where is your father?

221
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:07,091
Now Dad's gone missing, too.

222
00:16:07,591 --> 00:16:10,469
What?! Why? Who else is missing?

223
00:16:13,889 --> 00:16:15,849
Mayor, some of our men
saw Miss Aguas leave

224
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:17,101
right after Sir Raul.

225
00:16:17,935 --> 00:16:19,144
They left together?

226
00:16:20,771 --> 00:16:21,689
Where did they go?

227
00:16:21,772 --> 00:16:22,940
Outside Poblacion Ardiente.

228
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,150
[tense music playing]

229
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:37,788
[tense music playing]

230
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:57,683
-[screaming]
-[Belen] Raul!

231
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:02,021
-Aunt Belen.
-[screaming continues]

232
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:04,982
Aunt Belen, get the door ready! The key!

233
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:07,693
[screaming, sobbing]

234
00:17:10,988 --> 00:17:11,989
[screams]

235
00:17:15,868 --> 00:17:17,411
-[screaming]
-[door slams]

236
00:17:18,245 --> 00:17:19,413
[screams]

237
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:23,417
[Camia pounding on door]

238
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:28,422
[sobbing]

239
00:17:29,631 --> 00:17:31,050
[sighs] I guess…

240
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:34,762
it would be best if we go away for now.

241
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:36,180
We're moving away from here.

242
00:17:36,263 --> 00:17:38,766
It's late. You can just go tomorrow.

243
00:17:39,099 --> 00:17:43,479
No. We have to leave now.
A lot of people are on to me.

244
00:17:43,562 --> 00:17:46,690
I can't risk it. I have to hide Camia.

245
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:50,152
-[tense music playing]
-Camia? Who is Camia?

246
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:51,570
[suspenseful sting]

247
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:56,075
Raul, tell me the truth.

248
00:17:58,368 --> 00:17:59,995
Who is that woman?

249
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:06,835
[tense music playing]

250
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:29,274
Ivy?

251
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:53,632
Ivy?

252
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:02,182
[suspenseful music playing]

253
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:09,982
Raul, I've been suspicious for a while.

254
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:12,818
I didn't say anything because I trust you.

255
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:16,905
Who is that woman?
Why are you locking her up?!

256
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:26,790
Auntie, stay out of this. Okay?

257
00:19:27,416 --> 00:19:30,794
Don't worry. We won't trouble you anymore.

258
00:19:31,086 --> 00:19:33,255
And you won't see us again.

259
00:19:33,338 --> 00:19:35,757
Just don't say anything to anyone.

260
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:37,676
-But, Raul--
-No, Auntie.

261
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:40,012
You don't understand.
You don't know anything.

262
00:19:40,095 --> 00:19:41,722
[foreboding music playing]

263
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:48,103
Auntie, what are you doing?! Huh?!

264
00:19:48,353 --> 00:19:49,396
-What?!
-Raul!

265
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:51,523
-What are you doing?!
-I can't let you do this!

266
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:52,858
You don't understand!

267
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:54,818
You don't understand! Give me the key!

268
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:56,612
-Please stop, Raul.
-Give me the key!

269
00:19:57,779 --> 00:19:58,780
-[punches]
-[groans]

270
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:01,241
[Raul] Come on, Auntie!

271
00:20:01,325 --> 00:20:03,410
[groaning, crying]

272
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:11,376
Raul. Raul, Raul…

273
00:20:23,764 --> 00:20:25,891
[suspenseful music playing]

274
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:42,324
[lock disengages]

275
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:48,121
Camia…

276
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:53,835
Camia, I won't hurt you. Don't be afraid.

277
00:20:56,421 --> 00:21:00,884
I just want you to know
that nobody can keep us apart.

278
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:03,971
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[Camia screaming]

279
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:06,348
[muffled screaming]

280
00:21:07,391 --> 00:21:08,642
[Raul shushes]

281
00:21:12,771 --> 00:21:14,147
[suspenseful music playing]

282
00:21:20,862 --> 00:21:23,240
[unsettling music playing]

283
00:21:25,617 --> 00:21:28,537
[panting]

284
00:21:50,642 --> 00:21:51,727
[Diego] Ivy.

285
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:56,440
Ivy, what happened to you?
Where have you been?

286
00:21:58,191 --> 00:21:59,359
My mom…

287
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:01,445
What? Ivy.

288
00:22:03,947 --> 00:22:05,782
Ivy, Prianka's been dead for years.

289
00:22:10,871 --> 00:22:14,416
[suspenseful music playing]

290
00:22:17,836 --> 00:22:18,920
Ivy?

291
00:22:27,387 --> 00:22:28,847
[engine starts]

292
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:54,372
Emilia. We can't contact Raul.

293
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:58,710
And it turns out,
Ivy has gone missing with him.

294
00:23:00,587 --> 00:23:01,755
Coincidence?

295
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:09,137
In the world of traitors,
there is no such thing.

296
00:23:10,263 --> 00:23:12,099
I've been married to Raul for many years.

297
00:23:12,182 --> 00:23:15,102
And I know when my husband
is up to something.

298
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:17,896
[tense music playing]

299
00:23:32,953 --> 00:23:35,122
[phone ringing]

300
00:23:40,043 --> 00:23:41,086
[Jepoy] <i>Ivy.</i>

301
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,046
Ivy, you left all of a sudden.

302
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:44,756
The mayor and the governor
have been looking for you.

303
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:45,757
Where did you go?

304
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:48,760
I followed Raul.

305
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:52,139
<i>Jepoy…</i>

306
00:23:52,222 --> 00:23:55,475
[instrumental theme music playing]

307
00:23:57,310 --> 00:23:58,770
I saw my mom.

308
00:24:01,773 --> 00:24:04,442
I'm sure it was her.

309
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:11,533
But she ran from me.
I kept calling for her, but…

310
00:24:13,201 --> 00:24:15,120
I don't understand.

311
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:22,377
I couldn't catch up to her, Jepoy.

312
00:24:22,586 --> 00:24:24,629
But I'm sure that was my mom.

313
00:24:27,382 --> 00:24:29,801
Ivy, listen to me.

314
00:24:31,178 --> 00:24:33,930
Don't ever blame yourself
for what happened.

315
00:24:34,347 --> 00:24:37,851
What's important is that
we're sure your mom is alive.

316
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:40,562
I know what to do…

317
00:24:43,899 --> 00:24:45,692
now that I've confirmed Raul has her.

318
00:24:47,235 --> 00:24:49,404
<i>But I have to be careful, Jepoy…</i>

319
00:24:51,323 --> 00:24:53,325
now that I know my mom is still alive.

320
00:24:53,950 --> 00:24:56,953
[instrumental theme music playing]

321
00:25:04,878 --> 00:25:05,879
Mom…

322
00:25:13,511 --> 00:25:16,181
[instrumental theme music playing]

323
00:25:16,306 --> 00:25:17,224
[sniffles]

324
00:25:17,807 --> 00:25:19,226
Why, Mom?

325
00:25:22,395 --> 00:25:23,396
Why…

326
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:28,360
Why doesn't my mother remember me?

327
00:25:46,878 --> 00:25:50,423
We've been waiting for you, Diego.

328
00:25:50,507 --> 00:25:51,508
[giggles]

329
00:25:51,591 --> 00:25:52,842
Nanny, why did you wait for me?

330
00:25:52,926 --> 00:25:56,221
[Pandoy] Well, she's just been
so giddy over you and Ms. Aguas.

331
00:25:56,304 --> 00:25:58,139
-[laughing]
-Hey! It's not like that!

332
00:25:58,848 --> 00:26:01,476
It's really not like that!

333
00:26:01,559 --> 00:26:04,396
I'm just happy. So, Diego?

334
00:26:04,479 --> 00:26:06,523
Have you confessed your feelings to her?

335
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:09,025
Does our little Diego
finally have a girlfriend?

336
00:26:09,109 --> 00:26:11,152
No. That didn't happen.

337
00:26:13,571 --> 00:26:17,117
Nanny, after we talked,
she left right away.

338
00:26:17,325 --> 00:26:20,203
On my way home,
I saw her looking like a mess.

339
00:26:20,287 --> 00:26:21,371
She looked like she just cried.

340
00:26:21,454 --> 00:26:23,081
-What?
-And she said…

341
00:26:23,581 --> 00:26:25,041
she saw her mother.

342
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:28,712
What? Who? Prianka?

343
00:26:29,045 --> 00:26:30,588
I thought she's been dead for years.

344
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:31,965
Is she being haunted?

345
00:26:32,632 --> 00:26:34,467
Hey! Don't say that.

346
00:26:34,551 --> 00:26:39,139
Maybe she just missed her,
so she imagined things.

347
00:26:40,015 --> 00:26:45,937
I'm confused if she's referring
to Prianka Aguas or Camia Cruz.

348
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:52,110
Nanny, I have a hunch that Ivy
and Lily are the same person.

349
00:26:55,196 --> 00:26:59,784
Then, what do you plan to do now, Diego?

350
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:02,704
Are you going to investigate Miss Aguas?

351
00:27:03,496 --> 00:27:04,914
Are you still going to court her?

352
00:27:04,998 --> 00:27:07,208
[somber piano music playing]

353
00:27:08,209 --> 00:27:09,586
-[sighs]
-[Loring] Diego…

354
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:14,007
maybe you're falling in love with Miss Ivy

355
00:27:14,090 --> 00:27:16,343
because you think that she's Lily.

356
00:27:17,510 --> 00:27:19,095
What if that's not true?

357
00:27:20,138 --> 00:27:23,266
Would you still be in love with Miss Ivy?

358
00:27:31,107 --> 00:27:32,692
Nanny, where's Raul?

359
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:35,487
He's not here yet, Governor.
But you have a visitor.

360
00:27:36,196 --> 00:27:37,197
Emilia.

361
00:27:37,447 --> 00:27:38,865
-Hi.
-Ivy!

362
00:27:41,159 --> 00:27:43,286
I just wanted to ask
how your charity event went.

363
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:44,913
-Well?
-Oh.

364
00:27:45,121 --> 00:27:46,915
It was a success.

365
00:27:47,082 --> 00:27:50,710
The poor were so happy with my gifts.

366
00:27:50,794 --> 00:27:54,798
You're so used to acting
like you care for the poor.

367
00:27:55,882 --> 00:27:58,426
Of course. It's all for show, Ivy.

368
00:27:58,593 --> 00:28:00,804
It's all for publicity.

369
00:28:01,971 --> 00:28:05,183
Good point. But, don't
the press people ask you

370
00:28:05,266 --> 00:28:09,813
why you're not with your husband
most of the time?

371
00:28:11,648 --> 00:28:13,650
Of course they don't.

372
00:28:13,775 --> 00:28:16,444
The people are used to seeing Raul

373
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:18,488
popping up and disappearing.

374
00:28:18,988 --> 00:28:20,281
But in the end…

375
00:28:22,492 --> 00:28:24,285
he still comes home to me.

376
00:28:25,662 --> 00:28:28,748
Okay. So, where's Raul?

377
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:31,543
You know…

378
00:28:33,920 --> 00:28:36,798
I was about to ask you the same question.

379
00:28:38,341 --> 00:28:41,761
A lot of people noticed
that you and Raul left the party

380
00:28:41,845 --> 00:28:43,221
at the same time.

381
00:28:44,305 --> 00:28:47,350
Like you just vanished into thin air.

382
00:28:48,893 --> 00:28:54,357
You know, Ivy, what I hate
the most are traitors.

383
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:57,235
Are you trying to say something, Emilia?

384
00:28:57,944 --> 00:29:02,532
No, I'm not. How about you?
Are you trying to say something?

385
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:05,577
I don't like women flirting
with my husband.

386
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:08,705
Are you flirting with Raul?

387
00:29:08,955 --> 00:29:12,250
Flirting? You call that flirting?

388
00:29:12,333 --> 00:29:13,793
Did it ever occur to you that maybe,

389
00:29:13,877 --> 00:29:15,795
I was only being friendly
with your husband?

390
00:29:16,045 --> 00:29:19,257
Emilia, please don't make
your insecurities too obvious.

391
00:29:19,340 --> 00:29:20,383
[scoffs]

392
00:29:20,508 --> 00:29:23,553
Ivy, I'm not playing games here.

393
00:29:23,845 --> 00:29:25,180
Don't even think about betraying me

394
00:29:25,263 --> 00:29:27,557
because you won't like
having me as an enemy.

395
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:30,560
I'm not playing games, either, Emilia.

396
00:29:31,186 --> 00:29:33,938
And I am not the type of woman
who likes having affairs

397
00:29:34,189 --> 00:29:36,691
because I don't intend
on tainting my reputation

398
00:29:36,775 --> 00:29:39,360
just to sleep with your
good-for-nothing husband.

399
00:29:40,403 --> 00:29:43,948
And I won't pour money into your family

400
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:47,035
just because of a man like your husband.

401
00:29:47,744 --> 00:29:51,164
Do you want me to pull out
all my investments?

402
00:29:51,664 --> 00:29:53,333
Do you think your father would like that?

403
00:29:53,666 --> 00:29:57,086
Don't forget, Emilia,
Julio is all set to return.

404
00:29:57,921 --> 00:29:59,172
Keep that in mind.

405
00:29:59,839 --> 00:30:02,550
Project your insecurities
elsewhere, but not onto me.

406
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:06,429
[tense music playing]

407
00:30:27,283 --> 00:30:30,787
<i>I will find you, Raul,</i>
<i>no matter where you hide.</i>

408
00:30:51,266 --> 00:30:54,060
[unsettling music playing]

409
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:32,265
[suspenseful sting]

410
00:31:41,316 --> 00:31:43,234
[suspenseful music playing]

411
00:32:31,032 --> 00:32:34,118
Hello? Anyone home?

412
00:32:41,167 --> 00:32:42,627
[Belen] How may I help you?

413
00:32:44,003 --> 00:32:45,755
I'm looking for someone.

414
00:32:46,339 --> 00:32:47,966
Her name is Camia Cruz.

415
00:32:49,092 --> 00:32:50,134
Who are you?

416
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:52,971
I am Ivy Aguas.

417
00:32:53,179 --> 00:32:56,683
Camia Cruz is in our list
of missing persons,

418
00:32:56,933 --> 00:32:58,643
and the authorities are looking for her.

419
00:32:58,726 --> 00:32:59,811
Did you know that?

420
00:33:00,520 --> 00:33:01,562
I don't know anything.

421
00:33:01,646 --> 00:33:02,981
Hold on, ma'am.

422
00:33:03,982 --> 00:33:07,860
It's obvious that you're lying.
I can see it in your eyes.

423
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:11,781
Wait. Did someone hurt you?
What happened to that?

424
00:33:11,906 --> 00:33:13,157
It's none of your business!

425
00:33:14,075 --> 00:33:15,994
Let's just say…

426
00:33:17,370 --> 00:33:21,624
I can protect you
from whoever you're protecting

427
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:25,795
by not telling me where Camia Cruz is.

428
00:33:27,088 --> 00:33:28,548
You have my word.

429
00:33:28,881 --> 00:33:32,760
But if you don't tell me
where Camia Cruz is,

430
00:33:32,844 --> 00:33:35,972
mark my words, you will rot in prison.

431
00:33:36,055 --> 00:33:38,641
[suspenseful music playing]

432
00:33:42,770 --> 00:33:45,189
[voice breaking]
He told me her name was Jasmin.

433
00:33:45,523 --> 00:33:49,235
But believe me, I didn't know
he was planning something bad!

434
00:33:49,986 --> 00:33:54,991
Raul left with Camia last night
and went somewhere far away.

435
00:33:56,534 --> 00:33:58,786
Raul… Raul Torillo?

436
00:33:59,787 --> 00:34:01,205
He has Camia.

437
00:34:01,497 --> 00:34:03,916
[suspenseful music playing]

438
00:34:10,048 --> 00:34:11,799
<i>Raul, you bastard.</i>

439
00:34:14,802 --> 00:34:17,180
[tense music playing]

440
00:34:56,803 --> 00:34:58,679
[tense music playing]

441
00:35:29,919 --> 00:35:32,213
[tense music playing]

442
00:36:03,661 --> 00:36:06,247
[tense music intensifies]

443
00:36:18,718 --> 00:36:21,053
[mysterious unsettling music playing]

444
00:36:25,808 --> 00:36:27,059
[suspenseful sting]

445
00:36:28,644 --> 00:36:30,688
[breathing heavily]

446
00:36:33,524 --> 00:36:36,402
[suspenseful music playing]

447
00:36:42,783 --> 00:36:43,784
Papa?

448
00:36:52,752 --> 00:36:53,794
Emilia.

449
00:36:55,713 --> 00:36:56,756
Emilia!

450
00:37:04,472 --> 00:37:06,515
[breathing heavily]

451
00:37:08,059 --> 00:37:09,185
[gasps]

452
00:37:09,936 --> 00:37:12,146
[suspenseful music playing]

453
00:37:12,480 --> 00:37:14,774
[breathing heavily]

454
00:37:25,534 --> 00:37:27,912
[suspenseful music playing]

455
00:37:32,875 --> 00:37:35,169
[tapping sound]

456
00:37:42,009 --> 00:37:43,552
[carpenter] Oh. Good morning, Governor.

457
00:37:43,636 --> 00:37:45,346
Hey! What's so good
about the morning?! Huh?!

458
00:37:45,429 --> 00:37:47,139
You're already causing
a disturbance this early!

459
00:37:47,223 --> 00:37:48,391
-Get out of my sight!
-Yes, ma'am.

460
00:37:48,474 --> 00:37:49,558
Get out!

461
00:37:52,770 --> 00:37:55,564
[ominous music playing]

462
00:38:06,826 --> 00:38:07,868
Emilia.

463
00:38:10,496 --> 00:38:11,789
Is everything okay?

464
00:38:13,207 --> 00:38:15,334
Yes, Auntie. I'm okay.

465
00:38:22,091 --> 00:38:24,927
[woman] Congressman
Julio Ardiente has arrived.

466
00:38:25,011 --> 00:38:26,762
[supporters shouting indistinctly]

467
00:38:29,390 --> 00:38:31,350
[supporter 1] Señor Julio is here!

468
00:38:31,934 --> 00:38:33,352
[supporters whooping]

469
00:38:33,602 --> 00:38:35,146
[supporter 1] Señor Julio is here!

470
00:38:36,731 --> 00:38:38,441
[suspenseful music playing]

471
00:38:41,986 --> 00:38:43,195
[supporter 2] Congressman!

472
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:45,489
[supporter 3] Welcome back, Congressman!

473
00:38:46,699 --> 00:38:48,451
We missed you, Congressman!

474
00:38:51,162 --> 00:38:52,830
[supporter 1] Welcome back, Señor Julio!

475
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:54,248
[supporters] Welcome back!

476
00:38:54,332 --> 00:38:57,084
[supporters chanting]
Señor Julio! Señor Julio!

477
00:38:57,168 --> 00:39:03,549
Señor Julio! Señor Julio!
Señor Julio! Señor Julio!

478
00:39:03,632 --> 00:39:05,176
Señor Julio!

479
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:07,011
[Arnaldo] Welcome back, Grandpa.

480
00:39:07,094 --> 00:39:08,721
[Julio] Thank you, grandson.

481
00:39:08,804 --> 00:39:14,226
Thank you very much to the
people of Poblacion Ardiente,

482
00:39:14,602 --> 00:39:17,772
and most especially,
to all of you, my children.

483
00:39:18,481 --> 00:39:22,443
Thank you very much for your prayers.

484
00:39:22,526 --> 00:39:25,279
I wouldn't have gotten better
without them.

485
00:39:25,613 --> 00:39:27,114
Thank you, everyone.

486
00:39:27,990 --> 00:39:34,872
And now, I have returned, fully recovered,

487
00:39:35,206 --> 00:39:39,335
and even stronger than an ox.

488
00:39:39,418 --> 00:39:41,253
-[laughter]
-Long live Señor Julio!

489
00:39:41,420 --> 00:39:44,215
-Long live Señor Julio!
-Long live Señor Julio!

490
00:39:44,757 --> 00:39:48,594
I'm eager to assume my duties
and serve you.

491
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:53,099
Of course, we'll clean up
whatever needs to be cleaned.

492
00:39:53,808 --> 00:39:59,855
And if needed, we'll cut off
the horns of those devils

493
00:39:59,939 --> 00:40:03,609
who played king here during my absence.

494
00:40:03,692 --> 00:40:05,236
[suspenseful music playing]

495
00:40:05,694 --> 00:40:06,695
Viva Ardiente!

496
00:40:06,779 --> 00:40:08,197
[supporters] Viva Ardiente!

497
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:09,407
[supporter] Viva Ardiente!

498
00:40:09,490 --> 00:40:11,367
[supporters] Viva Ardiente!

499
00:40:11,575 --> 00:40:13,494
[suspenseful music playing]

500
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:23,295
Emilia. Emilia.

501
00:40:25,798 --> 00:40:27,299
I missed you!

502
00:40:28,092 --> 00:40:31,137
Aren't you going to give
your father a hug?

503
00:40:34,306 --> 00:40:35,975
-Hi, Papa.
-Come here.

504
00:40:37,560 --> 00:40:40,396
I missed you, Papa. I missed you.

505
00:40:40,479 --> 00:40:42,440
I missed you, too, Emilia.

506
00:40:42,523 --> 00:40:43,441
[chuckling]

507
00:40:43,524 --> 00:40:45,818
I missed you. Welcome back.

508
00:40:46,068 --> 00:40:47,695
-[sniffles]
-[laughing]

509
00:40:55,494 --> 00:40:57,872
You can't fool me

510
00:40:58,330 --> 00:41:03,377
with your crocodile tears,
hugs, and kisses.

511
00:41:03,752 --> 00:41:08,257
I know what you've been doing
while I was gone.

512
00:41:10,551 --> 00:41:12,178
[both faking laughter]

513
00:41:12,261 --> 00:41:13,345
[Emilia] Papa…

514
00:41:14,597 --> 00:41:16,891
Again, thank you all.

515
00:41:16,974 --> 00:41:19,185
Thank you for welcoming me
and for your prayers.

516
00:41:19,310 --> 00:41:20,978
Thank you very much!

517
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:22,730
[supporter] Long live Señor Julio!

518
00:41:22,813 --> 00:41:24,482
[in unison] Long live Señor Julio!

519
00:41:24,773 --> 00:41:27,818
[supporters chanting]
Señor Julio! Señor Julio!

520
00:41:27,902 --> 00:41:33,699
Señor Julio! Señor Julio!
Señor Julio! Señor Julio!

521
00:41:33,782 --> 00:41:36,660
Señor Julio! Señor Julio!

522
00:41:37,328 --> 00:41:38,704
Viva Ardiente!

523
00:41:38,787 --> 00:41:40,539
[in unison] Viva Ardiente!

524
00:41:40,831 --> 00:41:42,082
Viva Ardiente!

525
00:41:42,166 --> 00:41:43,709
[supporters] Viva Ardiente!

526
00:41:43,792 --> 00:41:44,877
[chuckles]

527
00:41:49,715 --> 00:41:52,134
[gloomy music playing]

528
00:42:25,793 --> 00:42:26,919
[gasps]

529
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:30,005
[shushes] Jasmin.

530
00:42:30,923 --> 00:42:36,053
Jasmin? Jasmin, wait. Listen to me.

531
00:42:38,264 --> 00:42:41,225
Nobody's after you anymore, okay?

532
00:42:41,809 --> 00:42:43,936
You don't need to run,
you don't need to hide.

533
00:42:44,019 --> 00:42:45,980
I'm right here, okay?

534
00:42:46,272 --> 00:42:49,567
As your husband, I will take care of you.

535
00:42:50,067 --> 00:42:51,986
I won't let anybody take you from me.

536
00:42:52,861 --> 00:42:53,904
Okay?

537
00:42:54,363 --> 00:42:57,783
We'll be okay here.
We'll be happy here, Jasmin.

538
00:42:59,410 --> 00:43:02,329
That's enough. Don't worry.

539
00:43:02,413 --> 00:43:03,914
You're safe with me.

540
00:43:06,250 --> 00:43:07,501
You're safe with me.

541
00:43:09,795 --> 00:43:11,338
[tense music playing]

542
00:43:11,964 --> 00:43:14,717
You might be hungry.

543
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:17,011
I'll make you something to eat.

544
00:43:17,386 --> 00:43:20,222
Okay? Stay here and rest.

545
00:43:23,517 --> 00:43:24,560
Just rest.

546
00:43:37,156 --> 00:43:41,410
No. This is not happening.
This is not happening.

547
00:43:41,869 --> 00:43:43,787
[cries] This is not happening.

548
00:43:43,871 --> 00:43:45,789
[unsettling music playing]

549
00:43:46,332 --> 00:43:47,374
[flicks lighter]

550
00:43:50,461 --> 00:43:54,381
This can't be happening.
This can't be happening.

551
00:43:57,176 --> 00:43:58,260
Emilia?

552
00:43:58,969 --> 00:44:02,306
Auntie, this is not happening, right?

553
00:44:02,556 --> 00:44:04,308
This can't be happening!

554
00:44:04,725 --> 00:44:05,684
Calm down, Emilia.

555
00:44:05,768 --> 00:44:08,062
Auntie, he cannot take
everything away from me!

556
00:44:08,145 --> 00:44:09,563
He cannot do this to me, Auntie!

557
00:44:09,647 --> 00:44:11,607
-Calm down, Emilia!
-No, Auntie!

558
00:44:11,732 --> 00:44:12,900
-Calm down!
-[yelps]

559
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:19,156
If there's one thing
I know about predators, Emilia,

560
00:44:19,239 --> 00:44:21,241
it's that they smell fear!

561
00:44:22,159 --> 00:44:25,496
You can't allow Julio to smell your fear!

562
00:44:26,413 --> 00:44:28,165
That was the downfall of your mother,

563
00:44:28,290 --> 00:44:31,502
and I'll be damned
if I let that happen to you.

564
00:44:33,462 --> 00:44:37,549
He may be Julio Ardiente,
but he's only just a man!

565
00:44:37,883 --> 00:44:41,512
Do you understand me, Emilia?
Do you understand me?!

566
00:44:52,398 --> 00:44:57,653
<i>It's time to find out if that</i>
<i>woman is with us or against us.</i>

567
00:44:57,736 --> 00:45:03,033
<i>You know very well what happens</i>
<i>to our family's enemies, right?</i>

568
00:45:03,117 --> 00:45:05,744
[Emilia] <i>Raul, I'm sure Papa</i>
<i>will have you killed.</i>

569
00:45:05,828 --> 00:45:07,663
<i>You better stay at your parents' place</i>

570
00:45:07,746 --> 00:45:09,039
<i>in San Ildefonso.</i>

571
00:45:09,373 --> 00:45:11,166
[Ivy] <i>San Ildefonso.</i>

572
00:45:11,250 --> 00:45:14,294
<i>That's where Raul</i>
<i>could be hiding my mother.</i>

573
00:45:15,379 --> 00:45:16,964
<i>Is there a problem, Diego?</i>

574
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:19,800
[Diego] <i>I won't let anything</i>
<i>happen to you.</i>

575
00:45:20,008 --> 00:45:22,636
<i>I will protect you from my family.</i>

576
00:45:25,556 --> 00:45:27,683
[theme music playing]
